t had established a network of unseen  safe havens for over 150 years  and many of them were right under  batman's nose  across those years they ruled the city  and enforced their world from the  shadows  using seemingly immortal chemically  enhanced assassins called talons to do  their dirty work  evidence of the court of all's dates  back to the 1600s  and the infancy of gotham sea the cabal  had been involved in key moments of  history  and had a hand in some of its greatest  upheavals there are even suspicions that  they were involved in controlling the  distribution of power in the sea  bruce wayne noted that after the death  of his parents at the hands of joe  chill he wasn't able to accept that it  had been a random act of violence  instead he believed there was something  bigger happening that he couldn't  identify  days before his parents were murdered  bruce found an owl's nest in his attic  and despite showing them away they would  always return  an older version of the nursery rhyme  mentioned heeding the signs that the  core of owls were watching  and this he thought was their warning to  thomas and martha wayne  young bruce followed the hunch but it  ultimately amounted to nothing  and taught him not to let his emotions  guide his investigations  however when analyzing alan's body he  found that his great great grandfather  also had numerous small puncture wounds  on his body more importantly  his bones had traces of a residue from a  metamorphic rock  just like the nursery rhyme beware the  court or vowels  rolling gotham from a shadowed perch  behind granite  and lime the mysterious court of owls  began its campaign against batman  after bruce wayne revealed plans to  revitalize the city  a major deviation from the court's  long-laid plans  it begins by murdering a gotham citizen  and framing batman's ally  dick grayson aka nightwing for that  crime using his dna  and then proclaiming that bruce wayne  would also meet his  end imminently during a meeting with  mayoral candidate lincoln march  bruce is attacked by a talent named  william cobb  but continues to believe that the  assassin is simply using the legend of  the court of owls  as an advantage however he's forced to  abandon skepticism when he's once again  assaulted by cobb  and pulled into an underground labyrinth  there  looking down on him from above are three  figures  wearing owl masks bruce attempts to play  to his advantage and hide in the shadows  but every turn leads him back to the  center where a towering owl statue bears  down on him  showing him that wherever he goes the  path always leads him back to the core  valves  he finds a room with its walls lined  with pictures of those the court has  used and killed  and the numbers are in the hundreds in  the labyrinth  batman is driven to the brink of madness  he begins to act on emotion  despair starts to creep in as he  realizes gotham is not his city  and it never was the rooftops he bounds  across  on his quest for justice belonged to the  court and the allies he thought he had  were manipulated by them  and all that he knew and believed he was  was what they allowed  batman is believed to be infallible but  he has been broken many times  at the hands of the joker bane and other  villains  the events of the labyrinth however are  arguably his most  thorough defeat he was physically and  mentally bested  and more importantly his entire  understanding of the world as he knew it  was undermined  but each of his defeats have  strengthened batman's resolve  and it's no different in his battle  against the court of owls with the  secret society confirmed as real and  dragged into the spotlight  batman defeats cobb and escapes the  labyrinth vowing to return to root them  out  showing that no one knows gotham like he  does but the court has prepared  they've created an army of warriors  brought back from death and enhanced to  do their bidding  the talons number in the dozens and each  one is sharpened specifically to tear  down batman  as bruce prepares to take on the talons  and the court further revelations show  just how deep the court's influenced ran  it's revealed that william cobb was  actually dick grayson's great  grandfather  more insidious however is that grayson  was also selected to be  italian as the circus his family was  part of delivered child athletes to the  court to serve them  perhaps the court's greatest achievement  was that it shook bruce wayne's faith in  his understanding of the sea  but despite this when the court launched  a full frontal all-out assault on wayne  manor e4  while owls may be the natural predator  of bats bats make their homes in the  depths of darkness that owls are  incapable of reaching  and after being chased away bats always  come back  batman's investigation takes him to the  willow wood home for children which was  established to help children suffering  from mental illness and neurological  disorders  the home operated until a sinkhole  destroyed a portion of it  and in the time following the truths  about the abuse and neglect that  children faced there came to light  there batman once again met lincoln  march who is revealed was a puppet of  the court of owls and knows batman's  true  identity march having turned on the  court was killed by a talent and brought  back to life using the same  magic that allows the talons themselves  to cheat death  the most ground shaking revelation  however comes when march reveals his  real name  thomas wayne jr bruce's brother  born early and with complications thomas  wayne jr  was supposedly put in the care of willow  wood to heal out of the spotlight  his healing took a turn for the worst  however when funds dried up  after the home's biggest donor martha  wayne was killed  the supposed brothers face off with  thomas wayne jr outfitted in an  advanced talent suit he tells bruce that  they were to share the sea  but instead bruce left him to rot and it  was the court that came to save him from  his torment  the battle between them ends with an  explosion in an abandoned building  bruce escapes but his would-be brother  is thought not to have been so lucky  although batman emerges victorious it's  with the knowledge that the court of  owls continues to operate  having suffered a setback the court puts  into motion their plan to recruit a  talent that got away  the grey sun even scarier it's revealed  that the core of owls  was just a small group that is  ultimately part of the parliament of  owls which exists purely to corrupt the  house of wane  the court and the parliament's resources  are vast and their roots in gotham are  deep and strong  the secret society continues to be a  threat and in fact  they are more powerful than most even  realize their centuries-old presence  affords them a unique advantage over  batman  and their wings could engulf gotham once  again at any moment  currently the role the court of owls  will play in gotham knights remains  unclear  but given the extent of their power and  the grip they have on gotham  whatever presence they have will likely  be a formidable obstacle for the bat  family  so there you have it the history of the  court of owls  and why they're to be feared if you want  to talk more batman with me you can find  me on twitter  h i'll see you later bat fans  [Music]
 

